Abinova clipart gallery — provenance and license
================================================

The PNG images in this directory are the legacy clipart set inherited
verbatim from the AbiWord source tree (abiword/user/wp/clipart/, as of
the AbiWord 3.1.90 snapshot).  Upstream AbiWord ships this artwork
under the project's own license: the GNU General Public License,
version 2 or later (see the top-level COPYING file).

Notable individual items:

- gnome*.png: border/decoration artwork from the GNOME project's
  clipart collection, distributed with AbiWord under GPL-2.0+.
- tux_bordelais.png: "Tux", the Linux penguin, drawn by Larry Ewing
  (lewing@isc.tamu.edu) with The GIMP.  Larry Ewing releases Tux for
  any use provided he is acknowledged as the original artist:
  "Permission to use and/or modify this image is granted provided you
  acknowledge me lewing@isc.tamu.edu and The GIMP if someone asks."
  This notice satisfies that acknowledgment.

The images are only installed when Abinova is configured with
--enable-clipart.
